title UC.26 - Security & Access Enforcement (Single Session Revocation, RBAC & OTP)

boundary "Browser\n(Device A)" as DevA
boundary "Browser\n(Device B)" as DevB
control "AuthRouter &\nRBACRouter" as Auth
control "SessionService" as Sess
database "RedisCache" as Redis
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
control "AuthMiddleware" as MW

== Flow 1: Single Active Session Enforcement via JTI Revocation (FR59) ==
DevB -> Auth : 1. POST /api/v1/auth/login (username, password)
Auth -> DB : 2. Verify user credentials & bcrypt password_hash
DB --> Auth : Valid user record (user_id, role_id)
Auth -> Sess : 3. register_active_session(user_id, ip_B, user_agent_B)
Sess -> DB : 4. SELECT jti FROM user_active_sessions WHERE user_id=user_id AND status='ACTIVE'
DB --> Sess : Existing active session (jti_A on Device A)
Sess -> DB : 5. UPDATE user_active_sessions SET status='REVOKED' WHERE jti=jti_A
Sess -> Redis : 6. SET blacklist:jti_A = true (EX 604800)
Sess -> DB : 7. INSERT INTO user_active_sessions (jti_B, user_id, ip_B, status='ACTIVE')
Sess --> Auth : Issued JWT token with jti_B
Auth --> DevB : 8. 200 OK (Access Token jti_B)

DevA -> MW : 9. Subsequent API Request with Authorization: Bearer <JWT jti_A>
MW -> Redis : 10. GET blacklist:jti_A
Redis --> MW : 11. true (Session jti_A is revoked)
MW --> DevA : 12. HTTP 401 Unauthorized (error='CONCURRENT_LOGIN_KICKED')
DevA -> DevA : 13. Clear LocalStorage JWT & redirect to /login

== Flow 2: Dynamic 2D RBAC Matrix Update (FR58) & Email OTP Recovery (FR60) ==
DevB -> Auth : 14. POST /api/v1/rbac/matrix (role_permissions_grid)
Auth -> Auth : 15. Verify Self-Lockout guard (preserve core it_admin rights)
Auth -> DB : 16. UPSERT rbac_permissions_matrix & INSERT audit_logs
Auth -> Redis : 17. DEL rbac:permissions:* (Invalidate cache immediately)
Auth --> DevB : 18. 200 OK (Permissions enforced immediately)
@enduml